    "summary": "Resistance to data centers in Alabama is concentrated in counties with adopted or pending moratoria: Baldwin (a 180-day moratorium with a unanimous commission vote), Morgan (a one-year moratorium extended in October, with more than 8,000 voters backing restrictions on a nonbinding ballot question) and Shelby (Chelsea, Westover, Helena and Harpersville pauses). Cullman and Calhoun (Anniston) also have municipal moratoria, while Jefferson County shows the most organized backlash, with Bessemer officials losing seats over the Project Marvel rezoning and several towns pausing projects; Lowndes and Talladega stand out for lawsuits, petitions and town halls. Not every county is moving against projects: Tuscaloosa (Brookwood approved a $3.2B campus), Chilton (rescinded its moratorium in October) and Montgomery lean toward approval, and many counties are scored high mainly on a county-wide base rate with no local evidence."
  },
